Disabling `proxy_buffering` can lead to unwanted behaviour. Unfortunately there is no way to set it dynamically inside NGINX e. g. based on POST requests or similar.

I just want to share another solution, which is possible due to the fact that NGINX respects `X-Accel-Buffering` to turn off buffering:

```ts
// middleware.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';

export async function middleware(request: NextRequest) {
  // Add no buffering header for server actions to allow streaming
  const response = NextResponse.next();

  if (request.headers.get('next-action')) {
    response.headers.set('X-Accel-Buffering', 'no');
  }

  return response;
}
```

