I'm running into some similar issues - with streamText as well as generateObject - and here are my observations:

- It works sometimes - I've gotten generateObject calls to successfully cache.
- Looking at the actual result.request.body content that's sent to anthropic, the cache_control parameter is not being passed to anthropic in some cases even when it's set. 
- In particular, I've noticed it work at the beginning of a conversation thread, and then not work *on the same message* after more messages are added on. 

My guess is that there are some cases that trigger some extra processing that loses the cache control parameter. 

The most minimal example I've been able to come up with involves sending a message with role 'data' - these messages seem to be ignored and not passed on, but the presence of one in the request still breaks cache control on OTHER messages.

