Opened #16752 to implement this.

The earlier attempt (#10463) was closed on design grounds — @lgrammel noted it *"bleeds the MCP spec into our tool spec"* by adding an MCP-shaped `annotations` field onto the core `Tool` type, suggested a generic `metadata`/`hints` property instead, and asked for tests + docs; @nicoalbanese *"feel[s] strongly that this would be best implemented in some kind of generic tool metadata."*

This PR is built around that feedback:

- **No changes to the core `Tool` type.** `@ai-sdk/provider-utils`, `@ai-sdk/provider`, and `ai` are untouched — all production changes are confined to `@ai-sdk/mcp`. The MCP spec never reaches the abstract tool spec.
- **Rides the existing generic metadata container** — the "generic tool metadata" both of you pointed at. The core `Tool` already exposes `metadata?: JSONObject` (which propagates to the tool call's `toolMetadata`); the MCP client just writes the hints into it under a namespaced `annotations` key. MCP's vocabulary is typed only inside `@ai-sdk/mcp`.
- **Namespaced, not flattened**, so the hints can't collide with sibling metadata keys and stay self-evidently MCP-sourced.
- **All four hints pass through**, but only as generic MCP-local metadata — so there's no cost to including `destructive`/`idempotent`/`openWorld` (and `destructiveHint` is the one this issue was really about, for confirmation-gating).
- **Cast-free consumer ergonomics + correct scoping** via two small helpers: `isMCPToolCall(source)` to detect MCP tools and scope logic (so a generic `toolApproval` doesn't accidentally gate non-MCP tools), and `getMCPToolAnnotations(source)` to read the typed hints without casting.
- **Tests, docs, and a runnable example** included.

Usage — gating execution on the hints via `toolApproval`:

```ts
import { getMCPToolAnnotations, isMCPToolCall } from '@ai-sdk/mcp';

await generateText({
  model,
  tools: await client.tools(),
  toolApproval: ({ toolCall }) => {
    if (isMCPToolCall(toolCall)) {
      const a = getMCPToolAnnotations(toolCall);
      if (a?.readOnlyHint === true) return 'approved';
      if (a?.destructiveHint === true) return 'user-approval';
      return 'user-approval';
    }
    // your own policy for non-MCP tools
    return 'approved';
  },
  prompt: '…',
});
```

