This should work for all "open models" which includes [Deepseek](https://console.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/publishers/deepseek-ai/model-garden/deepseek-r1-0528-maas)

[Seen here](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/open-models/use-llama):

<img width="210" height="95" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5287c2ac-8d88-47c9-a03b-28715222034c" />



```typescript
import { createOpenAICompatible } from '@ai-sdk/openai-compatible';
import { GoogleAuth } from 'google-auth-library';
import { generateText } from 'ai';

async function useLlama4Scout() {
  // Initialize Google Auth
  const auth = new GoogleAuth({
    scopes: ['https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform'],
  });

  // Get access token
  const authClient = await auth.getClient();
  const accessToken = await authClient.getAccessToken();

  // Create OpenAI-compatible client for Vertex AI
  const vertexOpenAI = createOpenAICompatible({
    name: 'vertex-openai',
    baseURL: `https://${location}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/${project}/locations/${location}/endpoints/openapi`,
    headers: {
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${accessToken.token}`,
    },
  });

  // Use Llama 4 Scout with 10M token context window
  const { text } = await generateText({
    model: vertexOpenAI('meta/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct-maas'),
    messages: [
      {
        role: 'user',
        content: 'Your long context prompt here...'
      }
    ],
    temperature: 0.7,
  });

  return text;
}

```
Currently Llama 4 is only supported on `us-east5` through this method. See [model locations](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/learn/locations) for details.

