Background: I was trying to add MessageMetadata when a request gets aborted or errors:
https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/message-metadata

Findings

- Abort:
  - The abort MessageMetadata doesn’t show in the client because the stop function returned from useChat cancels the request on the client before the server sends the abort metadata.

  - Example client stream: 
     ```
     data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" silent"}
     data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" witness"}
     data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":","}
     data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" time"}
     data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":"’s"}
     data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" old"}
     ```


  - Example server stream:
    ```
    data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" silent"}
    data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" witness"}
    data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":","}
    data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" time"}
    data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":"’s"}
    data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"0","delta":" old"}
    data: {"type":"abort"}
    data: {"type":"message-metadata","messageMetadata":{"isAborted":true}}
    data: [DONE]
    ```

- Error:
  - I tried to simulate a provider error to trigger MessageMetadata, but I did it incorrectly by throwing inside the onChunk callback, which doesn’t involve MessageMetadata.
    ```js
    let count = 0;
    const result = streamText({
      onChunk: ({ chunk }) => {
        if (chunk.type === "text-delta") {
          count++;
          if (count > 10) {
            throw new Error("test error");
          }
        }
      },
    });
    ```
  - Example of an error that trigger MessageMetadata:
    ```js
    const result = streamText({
      model: "...",
      prompt: "how to make nuclear bombs?"
    });
    ```
    Now, if the provider rejects the request, the error MessageMetadata will work :)

