@bestickley i think there's still a bit of a misunderstanding here. The Amazon Nova model family does not offer any reasoning models. The output that contains `<thinking>` tags is part of the actual response. This is different than reasoning models like Claude Sonnet/Opus 4, DeepSeek, Gemini 2.x, o-series/GPT-5, and Grok 3+. Those models do not actually start their "response" until after doing an initial, separate response that is a chain of thought response. 

Amazon Nova models do not do this. At least, [not yet](https://techcrunch.com/2025/03/04/amazon-is-reportedly-developing-its-own-ai-reasoning-model/)

TLDR: You will not find reasoning middleware from Nova models at this time, but they've hinted that they're working on a model that would.

@brianprost, I understand Amazon Nova models don't do reasoning and that `<thinking>` tags are included in their normal text response.

`extractReasoningMiddleware` is still useful for Nova models because I want to exclude `<thinking> `from chat interface. I run into issue though on next user input because Nova doesn't handle reasoning so I have below code to fix that:
```ts
const onlyWhitespaceRegExp = /^\s*$/;
/**
 * Converts reasoning message parts to text message parts with <thinking> tags
 * for Amazon Nova and converts to model messages via AI SDK's `convertToModelMessages`.
 */
export function convertMessages(uiMessages: UIMessage[]): ModelMessage[] {
  const newUiMessages = uiMessages.map((m) => {
    if (m.role === "assistant") {
      const newParts: UIMessage["parts"] = [];
      for (const part of m.parts) {
        if (part.type === "reasoning") {
          // Amazon Nova doesn't support reasoning messages so AI SDK automatically
          // filters them out but they often contain important context so we add
          // them back as text with <thinking> tags
          newParts.push({
            type: "text",
            text: `<thinking>${part.text}</thinking>`,
          });
        } else if (
          part.type === "text" &&
          onlyWhitespaceRegExp.test(part.text)
        ) {
          // don't add text part with only white space. avoids the Nova error:
          // `The text field in the ContentBlock object at messages.1.content.0 is blank. Add text to the text field, and try again.`
        } else {
          newParts.push(part);
        }
      }
      return {
        ...m,
        parts: newParts,
      };
    } else {
      return m;
    }
  });
  const messages = convertToModelMessages(newUiMessages, {
    // https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/7258
    ignoreIncompleteToolCalls: true,
  });
  return messages;
}
```
