# Workaround (temporary)
Until the root fix (https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/11509)  is merged and released, I’m using the following workaround to avoid duplicate stream initialization in React Strict Mode.

## Approach
Instead of relying on useChat’s built-in resume option, handling resuming manually.

useChat exposes [resumeStream()](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/reference/ai-sdk-ui/use-chat#resume-stream), which is internally used for resuming streams.
By disabling the built-in resume (`resume: false`) and calling `resumeStream()` exactly once, we can avoid duplicate resumes while preserving reconnect behavior.

## Implementation

```ts
// page.tsx

import { useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import { useChat } from "@ai-sdk/react";
...

type ChatProps = {
  autoResume: boolean;
};

export default function Chat(
  autoResume,
): ChatProps {
  // Create a ref to call resumeStream() once.
  const hasResumedRef = useRef(false);

  // Get resumeStream to manually control stream resumption
  const { status, resumeStream } = useChat({
  // Disable built-in resume to avoid double execution
  resume: false,
  ...
  })

  // Resume the stream if required.
  useEffect(() => {
    // If the auto resume is not required, skip resuming.
    if (!autoResume) return;
    // If the resumeStream has been called, skip resuming.
    if (hasResumedRef.current) return;
    // If the status is "streaming", skip resuming.
    if (status === "streaming") return;

    // Before calling the resumeStream, set the ref to true to prevent double resuming.
    hasResumedRef.current = true;
    // Call the resumeStream to resume the stream.
    resumeStream();
  }, [autoResume, resumeStream, status]);

  return (
    ...
  )
}
```
NOTE: Using localStorage or sessionStorage to persist the `hasResumed` flag could be safer, but this is intentionally kept as a temporary workaround.

