We're still experiencing this issue with `@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock@4.0.83` (latest as of 2026-03-25).

The root cause is in both `doGenerate` and `doStream`: when building `providerMetadata.bedrock.usage`, only `cacheWriteInputTokens` is included and `cacheReadInputTokens` is omitted.

**Affected code (both `dist/index.mjs` and `dist/index.js`):**

```js
// doGenerate — current (buggy)
...(response.usage?.cacheWriteInputTokens) != null && {
  usage: { cacheWriteInputTokens: response.usage.cacheWriteInputTokens }
}

// doStream — current (buggy)
const cacheUsage = (value.metadata.usage?.cacheWriteInputTokens) != null ? {
  usage: { cacheWriteInputTokens: value.metadata.usage.cacheWriteInputTokens }
} : void 0;
```

**Fix:**

```js
// doGenerate — fixed
...((response.usage?.cacheWriteInputTokens) != null || (response.usage?.cacheReadInputTokens) != null) && {
  usage: {
    ...response.usage.cacheWriteInputTokens != null && { cacheWriteInputTokens: response.usage.cacheWriteInputTokens },
    ...response.usage.cacheReadInputTokens != null && { cacheReadInputTokens: response.usage.cacheReadInputTokens }
  }
}

// doStream — fixed
const cacheUsage = ((value.metadata.usage?.cacheWriteInputTokens) != null || (value.metadata.usage?.cacheReadInputTokens) != null) ? {
  usage: {
    ...value.metadata.usage.cacheWriteInputTokens != null && { cacheWriteInputTokens: value.metadata.usage.cacheWriteInputTokens },
    ...value.metadata.usage.cacheReadInputTokens != null && { cacheReadInputTokens: value.metadata.usage.cacheReadInputTokens }
  }
} : void 0;
```

