## Workaround
The messages always seem to be in order, so in my case, I was able to simply render the LAST text part, and ignore the duplicates. I see from your screenshot that you have the same message being rendered, you might have to do something smarter than I did. But here's my code FWIW:

```typescript
                    {(() => {
                      // WORKAROUND: Render the LAST text part in the array -- there is a bug in the Vercel AI SDK
                      // that causes text parts to be duplicated when multiple messages are returned in a stream response.
                      // We assume that the last part is always the most recent.
                      // This will cause a momentary visual glitch while the previous duplicated text is shown,
                      // they'll disappear once the last message starts streaming.
                      const lastTextPart = [...message.parts]
                        .reverse()
                        .find((part) => part.type === "text" && 'text' in part && part.text);

                      if (lastTextPart && 'text' in lastTextPart) {
                        return (
                          <AIMessageContent>
                            <AIResponse>{lastTextPart.text}</AIResponse>
                          </AIMessageContent>
                        );
                      }
                      return null;
                    })()}
```

