Here is what we ended up doing... I am not 100% sure its the correct/best way but has been working for us and allows us to parse the stream parts on the UI and have type safety while allowing for granular control of handling what your stream may return.  This is with the latest version of v5 AI SDK:

```
const response = await fetch(your ai endpoint)

//handle errors and do stuff
if (!response.ok) {
  throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
}

if (!response.body) {
  throw new Error("Response body is null");
}

//a variable for accumulated text 
let accumulatedText = "";

// Use parseJsonEventStream and consumeStream from AI SDK
      await consumeStream({
        stream: parseJsonEventStream({
          stream: response.body,
          schema: uiMessageChunkSchema,
        }).pipeThrough(
          new TransformStream({
            async transform(part) {
              if (!part.success) {
                throw part.error;
              }

              const streamPart = part.value;

              // Handle text deltas
              if (streamPart.type === "text-delta") {
                accumulatedText += streamPart.delta;
              }
              // Handle data events coming from API (metadata, etc) this would be different depending on what you are sending from the server, we send id's and other metadata as its available.
              else if (streamPart.type === "data-metadata") {
                const metadata = streamPart.data;
                console.log(metadata)
              } 
              // Handle errors
              else if (streamPart.type === "error") {
                throw new Error(streamPart.errorText);
              }
            },
          }),
        ),
        onError: (error) => {
          throw error;
        },
      });

```
We ended up wrapping all this logic in just a simple function that we can call but you could clean it up and create your own custom hook to expose the onData/onWhatever callbacks as needed.

streamPart.type has the following so you could get whatever you needed and handle it as you saw fit in your application.

`"error" | "finish" | "start" | "file" | "text-start" | "text-delta" | "text-end" | "tool-input-start" | "tool-input-delta" | "tool-input-available" | "tool-input-error" | "tool-output-available" | "tool-output-error" | "reasoning-start" | "reasoning-delta" | "reasoning-end" | "source-url" | "source-document" | `data-${string}` | "start-step" | "finish-step" | "abort" | "message-metadata"`

For example with the approach above if you wanted to display reasoning you would just add conditionals for "reasoning-start", "reasoning-delta", "reasoning-end" and handle it as you saw fit.

