The warning you're seeing indicates that the xAI model you're using doesn't support JSON schema validation in the `response_format` parameter. [1](#1-0) 

## Why This Happens

When you pass a `responseFormat` with a `schema` property to an xAI model, the AI SDK checks if the model supports structured outputs with JSON schema validation. [1](#1-0)  If it doesn't, the SDK generates this warning and falls back to basic JSON mode without schema validation.

Looking at the xAI implementation, when a schema is provided but not supported, the code still sets `response_format` to `json_schema` with the schema included. [2](#1-1)  However, the warning is generated to inform you that the model may not strictly validate against your schema.

## What This Means

The warning is informational - your request will still work, but:
- The model will return JSON output
- The model may not strictly adhere to your schema structure
- You should validate the response yourself in your application code

## Similar Behavior in Other Providers

This is consistent with how other providers handle unsupported structured outputs. For example, in the OpenAI-compatible provider, when `supportsStructuredOutputs` is `false` and a schema is provided, it generates the same warning and falls back to `json_object` mode. [3](#1-2) 

The Groq provider has identical behavior. [4](#1-3) 

## Notes

The warning doesn't prevent your code from working - it's just informing you that the model won't enforce your JSON schema. Your previous error (with the empty enum array) was a separate issue that prevented the request from being sent at all. Now that you've fixed that, the request succeeds but the SDK warns you about the lack of schema validation support.

Wiki pages you might want to explore:
- [OpenAI Responses API (vercel/ai)](/wiki/vercel/ai#3.3)

