FYI, Google seems to follow an approach similar to OpenAI, where cache read tokens are a subset of input tokens. [Reference](https://ai.google.dev/api/generate-content#UsageMetadata)

So  a response with cached content will look like this:

```json
  "usageMetadata": {
    "promptTokenCount": 3076,
    "candidatesTokenCount": 26,
    "totalTokenCount": 3687,
    "cachedContentTokenCount": 2041,
    "promptTokensDetails": [
      {
        "modality": "TEXT",
        "tokenCount": 3076
      }
    ],
    "cacheTokensDetails": [
      {
        "modality": "TEXT",
        "tokenCount": 2041
      }
    ],
    "candidatesTokensDetails": [
      {
        "modality": "TEXT",
        "tokenCount": 26
      }
    ],
    "thoughtsTokenCount": 585
  },
```

And the price calculation for, say gemini 3 pro, would be:

- cache read tokens = `cachedContentTokenCount` = 2041
- input tokens = `promptTokenCount - cachedContentTokenCount` = 3076 - 2041 = 1035
- output tokens = `candidatesTokenCount + thoughtsTokenCount` = 26 + 585 = 611
- total price = (2041 * 0.2 + 1035 * 2 + 611 * 12) / 1000000 = 0.0098102

