We're hitting this in production with `@cloudflare/ai-chat` (WebSocket transport via `useAgentChat`) + `@ai-sdk/anthropic` on `ai@6.0.97`.

We already use `sendAutomaticallyWhen: lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithApprovalResponses` with `autoContinueAfterToolResult: false` as recommended. The issue is in `convertToModelMessages` itself:

**`ignoreIncompleteToolCalls: true` only filters `input-streaming` and `input-available` states** — it does not filter `approval-requested` parts. So if a `needsApproval` tool is pending approval and a new `onChatMessage` fires (e.g. reconnection, or the approval-responded trigger), `convertToModelMessages` produces a `tool-call` model message with no matching `tool-result`, and Anthropic rejects it.

Additionally, for `approval-responded` parts (approved but not yet executed), the switch at the tool-result generation stage only handles `output-denied`, `output-error`, and `output-available` — `approval-responded` falls through with no `tool-result` generated.

**Workaround:** We added a post-conversion sanitizer that collects all `tool-result` `toolCallId`s and strips any `tool-call` / `tool-approval-request` blocks from assistant messages that don't have a match:

```ts
const modelMessages = repairOrphanedToolCalls(
  await convertToModelMessages(strippedMessages, {
    ignoreIncompleteToolCalls: true,
  }),
);
```

[Full implementation](https://github.com/ferdousbhai/summon-ghost/blob/master/src/lib/agent/chat-helpers.ts#L130)

**Update to our [earlier workaround](#issuecomment-3958022788)** — we replaced the band-aid (`repairOrphanedToolCalls` that silently stripped orphaned tool-calls) with a proper fix that actually executes the approved tools.

## Root cause (two-part bug)

**1. `streamText` never calls `tool.execute()` for approved tools from message history** — only for tools in new LLM responses. When `sendAutomaticallyWhen` triggers a new `onChatMessage` after approval, the tool stays in `approval-responded` state, unexecuted.

**2. `convertToModelMessages` produces orphaned `tool_use` blocks:**
- SDK validation (~line 1349) considers approved tools "resolved" (removes from missing set)
- But `convertToLanguageModelMessage` (~line 1463) strips `tool-approval-response` for non-provider-executed tools
- The tool-result switch only handles `output-denied`/`output-error`/`output-available` — `approval-responded` falls through
- Result: orphaned `tool_use` reaches Anthropic → rejected

Also: `ignoreIncompleteToolCalls: true` only filters `input-streaming` and `input-available` — NOT `approval-requested` or `approval-responded`.

## Working workaround

Execute approved tools manually before `streamText` in `AIChatAgent.onChatMessage`:

```ts
private async executeApprovedTools(tools: ToolSet): Promise<number> {
  let executed = 0;
  for (const msg of this.messages) {
    if (msg.role !== "assistant") continue;
    for (const part of msg.parts) {
      if (!isToolUIPart(part)) continue;
      if (part.state !== "approval-responded") continue;
      const approval = part.approval as { approved?: boolean } | undefined;
      if (!approval?.approved) continue;
      const toolName = getToolName(part);
      const toolDef = toolName ? tools[toolName] : undefined;
      if (!toolDef?.execute) continue;
      try {
        const result = await toolDef.execute(part.input, {
          toolCallId: part.toolCallId,
          messages: [],
          abortSignal: new AbortController().signal,
        });
        (part as any).state = "output-available";
        (part as any).output = result;
        executed++;
      } catch (err) {
        (part as any).state = "output-error";
        (part as any).errorText = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);
        executed++;
      }
    }
  }
  if (executed > 0) await this.persistMessages(this.messages);
  return executed;
}
```

Then in `onChatMessage`, re-convert messages if any tools were executed:

```ts
const executedCount = tools ? await this.executeApprovedTools(tools) : 0;
const finalMessages = executedCount > 0
  ? await convertToModelMessages(this.messages, { ignoreIncompleteToolCalls: true })
  : modelMessages;
```

This ensures approved `needsApproval` tools actually run and produce proper `tool_use`/`tool_result` pairs. [Full implementation](https://github.com/ferdousbhai/summon-ghost/blob/master/src/lib/agent/chat-agent.ts).

