## Proposed Fix for Premature Tool-Call Emission

**File:** `packages/openai-compatible/src/chat/openai-compatible-chat-language-model.ts`  [[github](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)

**Root cause (detailed):** In the `TransformStream.transform()` handler, the code accumulates `toolCall.function.arguments` via `+= toolCallDelta.function?.arguments ?? ''`. After each delta, it checks `if (isParsableJson(toolCall.function.arguments)) { ... controller.enqueue({ type: 'tool-call', input: toolCall.function.arguments }) ... toolCall.hasFinished = true; }`. [[github](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)

For large tool args (e.g., ~5000+ char code strings with many `\\n`, `\\\"`), a prefix can pass `isParsableJson()` prematurely (looks like complete JSON), emitting a `tool-call` with **truncated string `input`** and marking `hasFinished=true`. Later deltas are ignored, causing incomplete tool calls. [[github](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)

**Why this fix:** Emit `tool-input-delta`s progressively (preserves low-latency UX), but defer the final `tool-call` (with parsed `input`) to `flush()` when the stream ends. This guarantees complete args, matches OpenAI's semantics (tool calls finalize at stream end), and avoids user middleware. [[github](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/12052)

**How it works:** 
1. Remove early `isParsableJson()` checks/early emits.
2. Always emit `tool-input-delta` on arg chunks.
3. Emit `tool-input-end` only in `flush()` (for all tool calls).
4. In `flush()`, `JSON.parse` args if possible (consistent object output).

**Exact code diff** (in `doStream()` TransformStream):

```diff
// In transform(), for new tool calls:
if (toolCalls[index] == null) {
  // ... enqueue 'tool-input-start'
  toolCalls[index] = { /* init */ };
  // ...
- if (isParsableJson(toolCall.function.arguments)) {
-   controller.enqueue({ type: 'tool-input-end', id: toolCall.id });
-   controller.enqueue({ type: 'tool-call', /* ... */ });
-   toolCall.hasFinished = true;
- }
  continue;
}

// For existing (in both new/existing blocks):
if (toolCallDelta.function?.arguments != null) {
  toolCall.function!.arguments += toolCallDelta.function?.arguments ?? '';
}
controller.enqueue({
  type: 'tool-input-delta',
  id: toolCall.id,
  delta: toolCallDelta.function.arguments ?? '',
});
- // check if tool call is complete
- if (isParsableJson(toolCall.function.arguments)) {
-   controller.enqueue({ type: 'tool-input-end', id: toolCall.id });
-   controller.enqueue({ type: 'tool-call', /* ... */ });
-   toolCall.hasFinished = true;
- }
```

**In `flush()` (add before providerMetadata):**
```diff
+ // Finalize all tool calls
+ for (const toolCall of toolCalls) {
+   controller.enqueue({ type: 'tool-input-end', id: toolCall.id });
+   let input = toolCall.function.arguments;
+   try {
+     input = JSON.parse(input);  // parsed object if valid
+   } catch {}
+   controller.enqueue({
+     type: 'tool-call',
+     toolCallId: toolCall.id ?? generateId(),
+     toolName: toolCall.function.name,
+     input,
+     ...(toolCall.thoughtSignature ? { /* ... */ } : {}),
+   });
+ }
```

**Impact:**
- ✅ Fixes truncation (full args always).
- ✅ Streaming deltas still work (partial args visible via `tool-input-delta`).
- ✅ No perf hit (one extra `JSON.parse` at end).
- ✅ Backward compat (existing non-streaming `doGenerate()` unchanged).
- ❌ Slight delay: `tool-call` arrives at stream end (~0.1-1s later for large args).



