The bug is definitely real on our end: we're carrying a `bun patch` on `ai@6.0.90` in production to get file `providerMetadata` (our download `fileId`) to survive streaming — without it, the metadata is gone by the time it reaches the client.

I think the "cannot reproduce" runs missed it because they fed a hand-built `file` chunk directly into `readUIMessageStream`, which only exercises the client read path (`processUIMessageStream`). The real drop is upstream on the **server** path — `streamText` → `toUIMessageStream()` — which those repros never run.

Here's a **full round-trip** repro on a clean `ai@6.0.90` (mock model → `streamText` → `toUIMessageStream` → `readUIMessageStream`):

```js
import { streamText, readUIMessageStream } from "ai";
import { MockLanguageModelV3, simulateReadableStream } from "ai/test";

const EXPECTED = { customProvider: { fileId: "file-12670" } };

const model = new MockLanguageModelV3({
  doStream: async () => ({
    stream: simulateReadableStream({
      chunks: [
        { type: "stream-start", warnings: [] },
        { type: "file", mediaType: "image/png", data: "iVBORw0KGgo=", providerMetadata: EXPECTED },
        { type: "finish", finishReason: "stop", usage: { inputTokens: 1, outputTokens: 1, totalTokens: 2 } },
      ],
    }),
  }),
});

const uiStream = streamText({ model, prompt: "give me a file" }).toUIMessageStream();
let filePart;
for await (const m of readUIMessageStream({ stream: uiStream }))
  filePart = m.parts.find((p) => p.type === "file");

console.log(filePart.providerMetadata); // undefined on 6.0.90 — expected: { customProvider: { fileId: "file-12670" } }
```

`providerMetadata` comes back `undefined`. The root cause is actually a **third** site I'd missed in my original report: `runToolsTransformation` (dist `index.mjs` ~5875 / `index.js` ~5951) builds the fullStream `file` part from `chunk.data`/`chunk.mediaType` but never copies `chunk.providerMetadata`. So the part is born without it, and the two downstream sites (`DefaultStreamTextResult` enqueue ~7390, `processUIMessageStream` ~5200) have nothing to forward. All three need the `...chunk.providerMetadata != null ? { providerMetadata } : {}` spread — patching only the last two (as our first `bun patch` did) still left streamed files broken.

