Excellent root cause analysis! The 30-second idle timeout on `api.z.ai` is definitely the culprit. Here's what's happening and some potential fixes:

## The Problem

GLM-4.7 generates tool_call arguments in a single batch (not streamed incrementally), creating a silence window that exceeds `api.z.ai`'s 30s idle timeout. This is fundamentally a mismatch between:
1. Model behavior (batch tool_call generation)
2. Upstream proxy timeout (30s idle)
3. Gateway routing (always to `api.z.ai`)

## Suggested Fixes

### 1. Gateway-side: SSE Keepalive (Recommended)

The Gateway could inject SSE comments during idle periods:

```typescript
// Every 10s of silence, emit a keepalive
setInterval(() => {
  if (Date.now() - lastDataTime > 10000 && !stream.closed) {
    stream.write(": keepalive\\n\\n");
    lastDataTime = Date.now();
  }
}, 10000);
```

This is a common pattern for SSE connections through proxies (Cloudflare, nginx, etc.) and would fix the issue for all Gateway-routed models.

### 2. Allow endpoint override

Expose a way to specify the upstream endpoint per-provider:

```typescript
providerOptions: {
  gateway: {
    zai: { baseURL: "https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4" }
  }
}
```

### 3. Workaround: Direct connection

As you discovered, using `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` directly to `open.bigmodel.cn` works. For production use until Gateway is fixed:

```typescript
import { createOpenAICompatible } from "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible";

const zhipu = createOpenAICompatible({
  name: "zhipu",
  baseURL: "https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4",
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.ZHIPU_API_KEY}` },
});

// Use zhipu("glm-4.7") instead of gw("zai/glm-4.7")
```

The 39s completion time you saw confirms the model just needs more time for large tool_call batches — no architectural changes needed on the model side.

---

This is a cross-cutting issue that likely affects other models with batch tool_call generation (DeepSeek, some Qwen variants). The SSE keepalive fix would benefit all of them.

