I've confirmed that the fix for this belongs in `runToolsTransformation` (`packages/ai/core/generate-text/run-tools-transformation.ts`), not in `toResponseMessages`.

`toResponseMessages` only builds conversation history for server-side multi-step execution (`maxSteps > 1`). When the multi-turn loop is driven by the frontend (via `useChat` + `sendAutomaticallyWhen`), the orphaned tool-call chunks reach the client directly from the stream — `toResponseMessages` is never in the path.

The approach: buffer provider-executed tool chunks (`tool-input-start`, `tool-input-delta`, `tool-input-end`, `tool-call`) in `runToolsTransformation` and only flush them when a matching `tool-result` arrives. If the stream ends without a result, the orphaned chunks are dropped. Client tool-calls and text content pass through unchanged.

I've validated this by patching `ai@6.0.0` locally — with the patch applied, the orphaned webSearch tool-call no longer reaches the frontend and the model retries the web search successfully on the next turn. Happy to open a PR if that would be helpful.

