I've confirmed this is a provider-side bug and have a working fix.

## Root Cause

The Vertex API's terminal streaming chunk for array args has `partialArgs` with the last value but **omits `willContinue`** entirely (the property is absent, not set to `false` or `null`):

```json
// Last chunk — partialArgs present, willContinue absent
{"partialArgs":[{"jsonPath":"$.operations[1].price","numberValue":0.5}]}
```

The `isStreamingChunk` check matches this (`partialArgs != null` is true), so it's processed as a regular streaming chunk. The `isTerminalChunk` check never matches because `partialArgs` is not null.

## Fix (3 changes in `google-generative-ai-language-model.ts`)

**1. `isStreamingChunk`**: Require `willContinue === true` for partialArgs chunks:
```diff
- const isStreamingChunk = part.functionCall.partialArgs != null || ...
+ const isStreamingChunk = (part.functionCall.partialArgs != null && part.functionCall.willContinue === true) || ...
```

**2. `isTerminalChunk`**: Also match when partialArgs present but willContinue absent:
```diff
- const isTerminalChunk = ... && part.functionCall.partialArgs == null && ...;
+ const isTerminalChunk = (... && part.functionCall.partialArgs == null && ...) || 
+   (part.functionCall.partialArgs != null && part.functionCall.willContinue == null && part.functionCall.name == null);
```

**3. Terminal handler**: Process final partialArgs before calling `finalize()`:
```diff
} else if (isTerminalChunk && activeStreamingToolCalls.length > 0) {
  const active = activeStreamingToolCalls.pop();
+ if (part.functionCall.partialArgs != null) {
+   const { textDelta } = active.accumulator.processPartialArgs(part.functionCall.partialArgs);
+   if (textDelta.length > 0) controller.enqueue({ type: "tool-input-delta", ... });
+ }
  const { finalJSON, closingDelta } = active.accumulator.finalize();
```

With this fix, array-typed tool args work correctly — `tool-input-end` and `tool-call` events fire, and `execute()` receives the full parsed args.

## Found the real fix

The core issue is in the provider's `flush()` handler in `google-generative-ai-language-model.ts`. When the stream ends (STOP), any active streaming tool calls are silently abandoned — `finalize()` is never called.

The Vertex API does NOT always send a terminal chunk (`willContinue: false` or absent) for the last function call in a response. The stream simply ends with `finishReason: STOP` while tool calls are still active. The provider's `flush()` handler closes text and reasoning blocks but **does not finalize active streaming tool calls**.

### Fix

Add tool call finalization to `flush()`:

```typescript
flush(controller) {
  // Finalize any active streaming tool calls that didn't get a terminal chunk
  while (activeStreamingToolCalls.length > 0) {
    const active = activeStreamingToolCalls.pop();
    const { finalJSON, closingDelta } = active.accumulator.finalize();
    if (closingDelta.length > 0) {
      controller.enqueue({ type: "tool-input-delta", id: active.toolCallId, delta: closingDelta, providerMetadata: active.providerMetadata });
    }
    controller.enqueue({ type: "tool-input-end", id: active.toolCallId, providerMetadata: active.providerMetadata });
    controller.enqueue({ type: "tool-call", toolCallId: active.toolCallId, toolName: active.toolName, input: finalJSON, providerMetadata: active.providerMetadata });
    hasToolCalls = true;
  }
  // ... existing text/reasoning block closing ...
}
```

### Additional fix: `isStreamingChunk` must require `willContinue === true`

The terminal chunk (last partialArgs with no `willContinue`) was matching `isStreamingChunk` because the original check only tested `partialArgs != null`. Fix:

```diff
- const isStreamingChunk = part.functionCall.partialArgs != null || ...
+ const isStreamingChunk = (part.functionCall.partialArgs != null && part.functionCall.willContinue === true) || ...
```

And `isTerminalChunk` should also match when `partialArgs` is present but `willContinue` is absent:

```diff
- const isTerminalChunk = ... && part.functionCall.partialArgs == null && ...
+ const isTerminalChunk = (original check) || 
+   (part.functionCall.partialArgs != null && part.functionCall.willContinue == null && part.functionCall.name == null);
```

### Also: Gemini generates phantom `.items` in JSONPaths for array fields

When a tool parameter is an array (e.g., `operations: z.array(...)`), Gemini sometimes generates `$.operations.items[0].description` instead of `$.operations[0].description` — leaking JSON Schema's `items` keyword into the path. Workaround: name the array field `items` so the phantom segment is harmless.

### Results with all fixes applied

With these patches on `@ai-sdk/google@3.0.62`:
- 17/19 receipts pass (2 failures are network errors, not accuracy)
- All receipts that ran successfully have $0.00 diff
- Progressive item streaming works end-to-end

