## 🔧 Solution Proposal

### Root Cause

The off-by-one error is caused by `doGenerateCalls.push(options)` being called **before** the array index lookup. After the push, `this.doGenerateCalls.length` is already incremented, so the first call accesses index 1 instead of index 0.

**Bug location (lines 46-52 and 57-63):**
```typescript
this.doGenerate = async options => {
    this.doGenerateCalls.push(options);  // ← length becomes 1
    // ...
    return doGenerate[this.doGenerateCalls.length];  // ← accesses [1] instead of [0]!
};
```

Same issue in `doStream` (lines 57-63) and in `mock-language-model-v4.ts`.

### Proposed Fix

**Option A (subtract 1):**
```diff
- return doGenerate[this.doGenerateCalls.length];
+ return doGenerate[this.doGenerateCalls.length - 1];
```

**Option B (capture index before push):**
```diff
  this.doGenerate = async options => {
+     const callIndex = this.doGenerateCalls.length;
      this.doGenerateCalls.push(options);
      // ...
-     return doGenerate[this.doGenerateCalls.length];
+     return doGenerate[callIndex];
```

### Files to Fix
1. `packages/ai/src/test/mock-language-model-v3.ts` — lines 52 and 63
2. `packages/ai/src/test/mock-language-model-v4.ts` — lines 52 and 63
3. `packages/ai/src/test/mock-embedding-model-v3.ts` — check for same pattern
4. `packages/ai/src/test/mock-embedding-model-v4.ts` — check for same pattern

### Impact
- **4-line fix** (or 8 if embedding models have the same bug)
- Restores deterministic multi-round conversation testing
- No API changes, fully backward compatible

Confirmation from a different angle: hit this exact bug while building a multi-step agent with HITL approval gates (`needsApproval: true` on a destructive tool). The flow is `generate -> validate -> security_review -> plan -> apply (paused for user) -> resume -> final text` — five model invocations for a single user turn, and each request to `/api/chat` creates a fresh `MockLanguageModelV3`.

With the array form, the first scripted turn (`generate_terraform`) is silently skipped, so `validate_terraform` runs against an empty pending slot and the whole flow looks broken in the UI even though the assertions in unit tests still pass. Took a while to track down because the apparent symptom is "the agent just... starts at validate?" with no error.

The function-form workaround using prompt inspection works well — actually nicer than a counter for this case because each `/api/chat` request gets a new model instance, so there's no shared state across requests:

```ts
function pickTurn(opts: LanguageModelV3CallOptions): LanguageModelV3StreamResult {
  const completed = new Set<string>();
  for (const m of opts.prompt) {
    if (m.role === "assistant" || m.role === "tool") {
      for (const part of m.content) {
        if (part.type === "tool-result") completed.add(part.toolName);
      }
    }
  }
  if (!completed.has("generate_terraform")) return turnGenerate();
  if (!completed.has("validate_terraform")) return turnValidate();
  // ...
}
```

Strong +1 on Option A or B from the OP — and on the fallback-to-last-entry behaviour for calls past the array's end. Out-of-bounds returning `undefined` is the second time the same flow breaks (apply success triggers a final turn the array didn't cover).

