## Proposed Solution: AbortSignal Propagation in Stream Consumer

### Root Cause
AbortSignal fires but ReadableStream cancel is silent — SDK consumers wait for a finish chunk that never arrives. Missing abort propagation in stream consumer and no timeout/fallback.

### Proposed Fix
Listen for abort signal in stream consumer and reject accumulated promises:

```typescript
async getFullText(): Promise<string> {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    if (this.abortSignal) {
      this.abortSignal.addEventListener("abort", () => {
        if (!finished) { finished = true; reject(new Error("Stream aborted")); }
      });
    }
    // Safety timeout
    setTimeout(() => { if (!finished) reject(new Error("Stream timeout")); }, 300_000);
    // ... stream processing with cancel handling
  });
}
```

### Testing Strategy
- Unit test: Abort signal rejects accumulated promises
- Unit test: Timeout triggers on stalled streams
- Integration test: Full abort flow with ToolLoopAgent
- Regression test: Normal streams still work

### Impact
- **Before**: Long-running agent runs hang silently for 30+ min, non-recoverable
- **After**: Proper abort with catchable error, clean resource cleanup

